<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield rises to 24.03 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield rises to 24.03 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month GKO discount Treasury bills rose to 24.03 percent annual at an auction on Tuesday from 22.56 percent at the last auction on March 25, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   Apr 1		Mar 25</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43K0307977     KZ43K2606970</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  500		  650</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 825		  1,400</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 471		  650</p>
<p> Average price			 94.25 pct	  94.66</p>
<p> Average yield			 24.03		22.56</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				July 3, 1997     June 26, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
